# Copy to `.env` in this folder (`server/.env`) and fill in secrets. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# =============================================================================
# Google "Continue with Google" (server-side OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow)
# =============================================================================
#
# --- A) Create credentials in Google Cloud Console ---
# 1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com/ → select or create a project.
# 2. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen → configure (External / Testing + test users if needed).
# 3. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID.
# 4. Application type: **Web application**.
# 5. Authorized JavaScript origins (optional for this flow; useful if you use Google Identity on the SPA):
#    - http://localhost:8080
#    - http://127.0.0.1:8080
#    - your production SPA origin, e.g. https://khudrapasal.360winx.com
# 6. Authorized redirect URIs — **must be the Django callback on your API host** (not the React app):
#    Local Django on port 8000:
#      http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/social/google/callback/
#      http://localhost:8000/api/auth/social/google/callback/
#    Production API:
#      https://YOUR-API-HOST/api/auth/social/google/callback/
#    The path is fixed: `/api/` (Django) + `auth/social/google/callback/` (see `core/urls/auth_urls.py`).
# 7. Copy **Client ID** and **Client Secret** into the variables below (or use a downloaded JSON file).
#
# --- B) Match redirect_uri with what Google expects ---
# Django builds redirect_uri as: `{OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE or request host}/api/auth/social/google/callback/`
# If you run behind nginx/HTTPS, set OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE to the **public** API origin (scheme + host + port).
#
# --- C) Frontend must start OAuth on the same API the user will return to ---
# If the SPA uses Vite's `/api` proxy to a remote server, OAuth runs on that remote server — put credentials
# on *that* server's `.env`, and register *that* server's callback URL in Google Console.
# For a full local stack (Django :8000 + Vite :8080), set in `web/.env`:
#   VITE_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api
#   VITE_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# so "Continue with Google" opens your local Django, not the proxy target.
#
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional: path to Google Cloud "Web client" JSON ({"web":{"client_id","client_secret",...}}).
# If id/secret are empty, the API also checks ../continue_with_google.json next to the `server/` folder.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS_JSON=

# Public API origin for OAuth redirect_uri (omit for local runserver — then request.build_absolute_uri is used).
# OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:8000
# Production example:
# OAUTH_REDIRECT_BASE=https://khudrapasalserver.360winx.com

# Where the API redirects the browser after success (?token=…&surface=…&redirect=…)
# FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:8080
# FRONTEND_URL=https://khudrapasal.360winx.com

# Default SPA path when OAuth `next` is omitted (align with customer home).
# REDIRECT_AFTER_LOGIN=/portal

# JWT / GIS token verification uses the same audience as the Web client ID unless overridden:
# GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN_AUDIENCE=

# CORS: SPA (FRONTEND_URL) calls the API on another host. Defaults allow all origins + explicit list.
# For stricter production: DJANGO_CORS_ALLOW_ALL=false and set CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS to your SPA origin(s).
# DJANGO_CORS_ALLOW_ALL=true
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://khudrapasal.360winx.com,https://staging.example.com
